Turkish + English Prompt-Injection Benchmark — data licensing

The files en.jsonl and tr.jsonl combine material under different licenses. Each row's `source` field says
which applies to it.

- source "hand-written": written for this benchmark by the GuardBee team.
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Attribution: "GuardBee Prompt-Injection Benchmark" (https://github.com/GuardBee/guardbee-mcp/tree/main/packages/injection-bench).

- source "Lakera/gandalf_ignore_instructions": https://huggingface.co/datasets/Lakera/gandalf_ignore_instructions
  License: MIT. Copyright (c) Lakera AI.

- source "deepset/prompt-injections": https://huggingface.co/datasets/deepset/prompt-injections
  License: Apache License 2.0. Copyright deepset GmbH.

- source "jackhhao/jailbreak-classification": https://huggingface.co/datasets/jackhhao/jailbreak-classification
  License: Apache License 2.0.

- source "OpenAssistant/oasst2": https://huggingface.co/datasets/OpenAssistant/oasst2
  License: Apache License 2.0. Copyright LAION / OpenAssistant contributors.

Rows with a `translation` field are machine translations into Turkish of rows from the sources above. They were
made with Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-tc-big-en-tr (CC BY 4.0, https://huggingface.co/Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-tc-big-en-tr) and
remain under the license of their source. Changes from the originals: whitespace normalized, the English text
translated, de-duplicated, and labels mapped to attack/benign as described in the README.

The compilation (selection, labels, splits, technique tags) is CC BY 4.0. No row is meant to contain real
credentials or personal data; the tests check that none passes the identifier checksums.
